<title>USA: TABLE - Elscint Ltd Q2 shr falls to $0.13.</title>
<headline>TABLE - Elscint Ltd Q2 shr falls to $0.13.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-08-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>ELSCINT LTD AND SUBSIDIARY COS</p>
<p>(UNAUDITED, in thousands except earnings per share amounts)</p>
<p>					  six months	three months</p>
<p>					 ended June 30,  ended June 30,</p>
<p>					1997     1996     1997     1996</p>
<p> net revenues		 $147,429 $148,115  $77,061  $75,448</p>
<p>research and development</p>
<p>  costs			   13,698   13,128    6,957    6,704</p>
<p> operating profit		4,225    4,335    2,962    1,485</p>
<p>finance (expenses) income</p>
<p>  - net			  (1,464)	924	114	256</p>
<p> other (loss) income - net  (1,175)   1,861    (714)    2,306</p>
<p> net income			1,346    6,535    2,122    3,975</p>
<p> earnings per share	     0.08     0.41     0.13     0.25</p>
<p>weighted average number of</p>
<p>ordinary shares and ordinary</p>
<p>share equivalents</p>
<p>  outstanding		   16,043   16,080   16,039   16,049</p>
<p>Note: The company's net income for the second quarter of 1996 includes $2.3 million resulting mainly from a patent dispute settlementy and from the sale of certain technologies.</p>
<p>Net income in the 1997 quarter was impacted by expenses of $0.4 million resulting from the establishment of ELGEMS, the joint venture company established by Elscint and GE Medical Systems which began operations in Israel on July 1.</p>
<p>The company said it expects it will incur additional losses on equity base in the third and fourth quarters resulting from transition and start-up costs associated with the joint venture company.</p>
<p>It also said it expects to begin generating positive financial results from the venture in in the beginning of next year.</p>
</text>
